.th DOC I June/77
.sh NAME
doc \*- documentation enquiry facility
.sh SYNOPSIS
doc [command]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it doc
is used to enquire from the database created by
.it mod
(VIII).
The main use of this database is to document changes and local peculiarities
for a particular installation.
.sp
.it doc
is designed for interactive use but, since it uses standard input
and output, it can be used in more cunning ways.
.sp
Keying a word produces a list of titles which are
linked to this word. Keying a title number results in the
display of the title and its abstract.
.sp
As well:
.sp
	lk = list keywords;
.br
	lt = list all titles;
.br
	la = list everything;
.br
	carriage return = list commands;
.br
	rubout = return to command level;
.br
	control D = exit.
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 25
/usr/pub/keywords
/usr/pub/keylinks
/usr/pub/titles
/usr/pub/abstracts
.fi
.dt
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
self-explanatory
.sh "SEE ALSO"
mod (VIII)
.sh AUTHOR
Peter Hewitt (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
Obtaining hard copy is messy : commands should allow shell-like
redirection.
